rsi community of Gujarat. It is made by cooking chicken or mutton with a mixture of lentils and vegetables. This is served with caramelised rice and fried onions. The dish was adopted during the British Raj into Anglo-Indian cuisine. A version of the dish has become a standard type of curry in the United Kingdom."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dhansak"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhansak"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Parsi cuisine","cuisine/parsi-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Cumin seed","ingredient/cumin-seed"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Gourd","ingredient/gourd"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Lentil","ingredient/lentil"],["Pumpkin","ingredient/pumpkin"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"ParsiCuisine.com","ref":"site/parsicuisine-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"parsicuisine.com","note":"Long-running community recipe site devoted to Parsi Zoroastrian cooking.","url":"https://www.parsicuisine.com/parsicuisine-com/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Parsi cuisine","links":[["Pathia","dish/pathia"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d8/Dhansak.JPG/500px-Dhansak.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Miansari66","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhansak.JPG"}},"dish/dre-si":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dre-si","n":"Dre-si","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Tibetan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dé-si is a sweet dish in Tibetan cuisine made with rice that is cooked in unsalted butter and mixed with raisins, droma (a tuber found in Tibet), dates and nuts. This dish is usually served only on Losar (Tibetan new year)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dre-si"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dre-si"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Tibetan c