f Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Bell's (restaurant)","dish/bell-s-restaurant"],["Belmond Le Manoir aux Quat'Saisons","dish/belmond-le-manoir-aux-quat-saisons"],["Beluga (restaurant)","dish/beluga-restaurant"],["Berowra Waters Inn","dish/berowra-waters-inn"],["Beurre maître d'hôtel","dish/beurre-maitre-d-hotel"],["Beurre manié","dish/beurre-manie"],["Bisque (food)","dish/bisque-food"],["Bistro 990","dish/bistro-990"],["Bistro Agnes","dish/bistro-agnes"],["Bistro Jeanty","dish/bistro-jeanty"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/df/Lucien_NYC.jpg/500px-Lucien_NYC.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Transpoman","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucien_NYC.jpg"}},"ingredient/dark-rum":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/dark-rum","n":"Dark rum","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Rum is a liquor made by fermenting and then distilling sugarcane molasses or sugarcane juice. The distillate, initially a clear liquid, is often aged in barrels. Rum originated in the Caribbean in the 17th century, where it was likely to have been first created by enslaved people on sugar plantations, but has come to be produced in nearly every major sugar-producing region of the world."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-dark-rum"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_rum"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Hungarian cuisine","cuisine/hungarian-cuisine",[["Rigójancsi","dish/rigojancsi"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Chocolate","ingredient/chocolate"],["Egg white","ingredient/egg-white"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Icing","ingredient/icing"],["Jam","ingredient/jam"],["Sponge cake","ingredient/sponge-cake"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}]},"ingredient/goshtaab":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/goshtaab","n":"Goshtaab","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Goshtaab, also spelled goshtaba, is a traditional Kashmiri dish that holds a significant place in the region's culinary heritage. Often referred to as the \"king of Kashmiri wazwan,\" goshtab is a rich and aromatic meatball curry made from finely minced mutton, yogurt, and a blend of spices. It is typically served as a final course in the traditional multi-course Kashmiri feast known as wazwan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-goshtaab"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goshtaab"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Kashmiri cuisine","cuisine/kashmiri-cuisine",[["Wazwan","dish/wazwan"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Rogan josh","ingredient/rogan-josh"],["Seekh kebab","ingredient/seekh-kebab"],["Tabak maaz","ingredient/tabak-maaz"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/ac/Goshtaba_wazwan.jpg/500px-Goshtaba_wazwan.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Oniongas","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goshtaba_wazwan.jpg"}},"ingredient/kirschwasser":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/kirschwasser","n":"Kirschwasser","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Kirschwasser, or just Kirsch (German: [kɪʁʃ]; the term used in Switzerland and France, less so in Germany), is a clear, colourless brandy from Germany, Switzerland, and France, traditionally made from double distillation of morello cherries. It is now also made from other kinds of cherries. The cherry stones are included in the fermentation process, not removed beforehand. Unlike cherry liqueurs and cherry brandies, Kirschwasser is not sweet. It is sometimes distilled from fermented cherry juice."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-kirschwasser"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirschwasser"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine",[["Zuger Kirschtorte","dish/zuger-kirschtorte"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Butter cream","ingredient/butter-cream"],["Hazelnut","ingredient/hazelnut"],["Kirsch","ingredient/kirsch"],["Meringue","ingredient/meringue"],["Sponge cake","ingredient/sponge-cake"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/4/4e/Fuersteneck_Kirschwasser.jpg","w":500,"h":1072,"by":"User:Mahlum","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fuersteneck_Kirschwasser.jpg"}},"dish/s-ll-k":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/s-ll-k","n":"Şıllık","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Turkish cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Şıllık is a Turkish dessert crepe that is a specialty of the southeastern Urfa province. It is a thin dough made of milk and flour, similar to a crepe, filled with ground walnuts and topped with simple syrup and chopped pistachio. Some versions of the filling may include a mix of walnut and pistachio. Butter or Turkish grape molasses may optionally be added to the simple syrup sauce. Traditionally, lamb tail fat was used to fry the crepes. In Turkish the word şıllık means slut or hussy, so some women in the conservative province of Urfa are not comfortable ordering the dessert by name, preferring instead to allow a male relative to order it for them or simply asking for \"that dessert\"."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-s-ll-k"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%9E%C4%B1ll%C4%B1k"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Urfa butter","ingredient/urfa-butter"],["Walnut","ingredient/walnut"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Ozlem's Turkish Table","ref":"site/ozlemsturkishtable-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ozlemsturkishtable.com","note":"Turkish-born cook and teacher Ozlem Warren's blog of home-style Turkish recipes.","url":"https://ozlemsturkishtable.com/tag/turkish-recipes/page/9","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Turkish cuisine","links":[["Adana kebabı","dish/adana-kebab"],["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bici bici","dish/bici-bici"],["Boortsog","dish/boortsog"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Çiğ köfte","dish/cig-kofte"],["Çökertme kebabı","dish/cokertme-kebab"],["Dede (restaurant)","dish/dede-restaurant"],["Doner kebab","dish/doner-kebab"],["Düğün çorbası","dish/dugun-corbas"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["İskender kebap","dish/iskender-kebap"],["Kavurma","dish/kavurma"],["Keşkek","dish/keskek"],["Kuru fasulye","dish/kuru-fasulye"],["Kyopolou","dish/kyopolou"],["Mesir macunu","dish/mesir-macunu"],["Nevzine tatlısı","dish/nevzine-tatl-s"],["Ntolmás","dish/ntolmas"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Piyaz","dish/piyaz"],["Qatlama","dish/qatlama"],["Rakı","dish/rak"],["Sofra (restaurant)","dish/sofra-restaurant"],["Stuffed leaves","dish/stuffed-leaves"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Stuffed squash","dish/stuffed-squash"],["Stuffed tomatoes","dish/stuffed-tomatoes"],["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"],["Yayla çorbası","dish/yayla-corbas"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8a/%C5%9E%C4%B1ll%C4%B1k_dessert_served_at_Hac%C4%B1baba_in_%C5%9Eanl%C4%B1urfa%2C_full_plate_view.jpg/500px-%C5%9E%C4%B1ll%C4%B1k_dessert_served_at_Hac%C4%B1baba_in_%C5%9Eanl%C4%B1urfa%2C_full_plate_view.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Kutlusafa","lic":"CC BY 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%9E%C4%B1ll%C4%B1k_dessert_served_at_Hac%C4%B1baba_in_%C5%9Eanl%C4%B1urfa%2C_full_plate_view.jpg"}},"ingredient/urfa-butter":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/urfa-butter","n":"Urfa butter","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Urfa butter, also called Urfa clarified butter (Turkish: Urfa sadeyaği), is a type of clarified butter made from sheep's milk that is distinct to the Turkish city of Urfa and the surrounding region. It is produced from the milk of the Üveysi sheep pastured on the southern outskirts of the Karaca Dağ and on the Tektek Dağ. The plants growing in these hilly regions form part of the sheep's diet and impart a slightly distinct flavor to their milk. Like other sheep's milk products, Urfa butter has a high percentage of milk fat. Besides Urfa itself, Urfa butter is also made in other parts of Şanlıurfa province, such as Siverek, Viranşehir, Ceylanpınar, and Harran."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-urfa-butter"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urfa_butter"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Şıllık","dish/s-ll-k"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Walnut","ingredient/walnut"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}]}}